Every orebody is variable. Changes in mineralogy, texture, hardness, liberation and chemistry influence how ore behaves when it reaches the processing plant. These variations directly affect recovery, throughput, energy consumption, water use, operating cost and ultimately the value delivered from every tonne of ore.
 
Mining operations already generate enormous amounts of geological, mineralogical, geometallurgical and plant data. But this knowledge often exists across different datasets, systems and disciplines. Geomet 360 connects these pieces to answer one powerful question: How will this ore behave when it reaches the plant — and what does that mean for the business?
 
Geomet 360 is an AI-powered geometallurgical agent that connects mineralogy, ore characteristics, geometallurgical data, domain knowledge and historical processing response. It creates a dynamic link between what we know about the orebody and what we know about plant performance.
 
Imagine knowing the processing risk before the ore reaches the plant. Geomet 360 understands the ore’s mineralogical and geometallurgical characteristics, identifies similar material processed historically, connects this information with processing models and anticipates its likely behaviour. What recovery can we expect? Will throughput be constrained? What is driving the response? And what actions could be considered before that material reaches the plant?
 
This shifts decision-making from reactive to proactive. Instead of discovering difficult ore after throughput drops or recovery is lost, teams gain earlier visibility of potential processing constraints. Mine planners, geologists and metallurgists can use a shared view of expected ore behaviour to support better sequencing, blending and processing decisions.
 
The business opportunity is significant. More predictable feed can mean more stable production, improved recovery, fewer unexpected throughput losses and better use of plant capacity. Understanding ore behaviour earlier can also help target energy, water and reagent consumption more effectively, supporting lower unit processing costs and improved resource efficiency.
 
Geomet 360 also allows users to interact with this intelligence conversationally. A user can simply ask, “What will happen when this ore reaches the plant?” “Why is recovery expected to decrease?” “Where is our processing risk next week?” or “Have we processed similar material before?” The agent connects the question to underlying data, models and historical plant response, providing not just an answer, but the evidence and context behind it.
 
This creates the foundation for a dynamic geometallurgical model. As ore moves through the operation, predicted behaviour can be compared with actual plant performance. The actual response becomes new knowledge, continuously strengthening the connection between the orebody and the plant.
 
Ultimately, Geomet 360 connects ore knowledge to business value. It helps operations understand variability earlier, reduce uncertainty between mine and plant, protect recovery and throughput, improve planning confidence and make better use of energy, water and other processing resources.
 
Geomet 360 creates a 360-degree view of the ore — connecting what it is, how it will behave, what it will cost to process, what value it can deliver, and what we can learn from the outcome.
 
Know the ore. Predict the performance. Protect the value. Geomet 360.

 
